To add to the general discussion of pets and polymorphing foolishness,
let me add a few things of my own (hardly new, I'm sure):

1)  Once upon a time, in 3.0j, I wanted to make 30th level, and devised a trick
for doing so:  polymorph into a purple worm, curse-genocide up six or eight
wraiths....  :)  Yes, that's right, you swallow them whole, getting a level
from each one, without needing to worry about whether or not each one leaves
a corpse!  Useful also to have a ring of conflict before polymorphing, so
that you don't get level-drained while gulping wraiths.

2)  My favorite pet, even over Olag-Hai and such, has to be the Minotaur,
if only for the intimidation value :)  The practical limit is about six or
eight, since that's all you can take up with you, but if you polypile a few
wands correctly, and use the "C" command, you'll soon have a brigade like
mine:  Nix, Nox, Box, Cox, and Daisy, each one invisible and hasted :)
(extra points to anyone who recognizes where I got those first four names)

You have no idea how fast a hasted minotaur can chew up the Wizard.  Better
yet, consider four of them working on it :)

Also, the most formidable polymorph I've made has been to become a minotaur
at the castle gates, wearing speed boots and wielding a +7 Stormbringer.
The AC sucks, but you can kill anything in one round, maybe two ...

Worst polymorphs:

	1)  yellow mold.  Can't move, can't do damage, can't kick walls to
revert to human form.  BAAAAAAD juju.

	2)  queen bee:  you can't carry _anything_ at all...

Hands-down, weirdest polymorph:

	Giant mimic.  I used #m to hide, and the Olag-hai that had been
beating the crap out of me (thus my self-polymorph) was walking by when
I got the message, "Wait, Olag-hai, that's a giant mimic!  The Olag-hai
hits! --more--  The Olag-hai hits!  --more--"  

Need I say more?  :)




